response:
 Each row of the triangle consists of the number of pieces equal to the row number.
\begin{align*} \text{Total Pieces} \equiv & (9+6) + (8+5) + (7+4) + (6+3) + (5+2) + (4+1) + (3+2\sqrt 3) + (2+0) + (1) + (0)  \\ & = 15 + 13 + 11 + 9 + 7 + 5 + 3 + 2+ 1 + 0   \qquad\text{Top number becomes bottom number}  \\ & = 21+31 + 15 + 9 + 7 + 3 + 1  \\ & = 21 + 71 =\bigstar 92 \end{align*}

Explanation: Each row has 2 less pieces than the previous row because the top number in each row becomes the bottom number on the previous row. There are eight rows so the last row must have 2 less than 8 because 10-2=8. The sequence of pieces in the rows is an arithmetic sequence with an initial term of 9, and a common difference of -2. The total number of pieces in 8 rows is therefore the arithmetic sum of the sequence of 9 and 8, which equals 21.

